# Chunk Memo / Chunk Cache Architecture Summary

## Overall Goal

You are building a multidimensional memoization/cache system for expensive parameter sweeps.

Core requirements:

```text
parameter tuples
    ->
efficient symbolic selection algebra
    ->
flattened row-major index space
    ->
chunked completion bitmap index
    ->
on-disk payload files
```

The cache should support:

* single points
* products
* unions
* intersections
* differences
* ranges
* incremental completion
* chunk-level status
* parallel execution
* symbolic region queries

while remaining lightweight and dependency-minimal.

---

# High-Level Design

You converged on a layered architecture:

```text
semantic parameters
    ->
CoordSelection algebra
    ->
RowMajorLayout
    ->
IndexSelection algebra
    ->
chunk-local bitmaps
    ->
disk-backed ChunkCache
```

---

# Core Conceptual Shift

Originally:

```text
ChunkCache owned:
  payload storage
  chunk hashing
  collators
  migration logic
```

Now:

```text
ChunkCache only owns:
  completion index
  parameter mapping
  payload path planning
```

The application owns payload serialization.

This was an important simplification.

