---

# Important Design Principles You Settled On

## 1. Separate semantic values from positional coordinates

Critical insight.

---

## 2. Symbolic algebra first

Avoid enumerating huge spaces whenever possible.

---

## 3. Chunking only exists in flat index space

Not in coordinate space.

---

## 4. Cache tracks completion, not payload semantics

Payload format belongs to the application.

---

## 5. Keep the backend minimal

You intentionally moved away from:

* heavy database systems
* roaring bitmap complexity
* over-general chunk metadata systems

toward:

```text
simple symbolic compiler
+
simple bitmap index
+
filesystem payloads
```

which matches your actual scale much better.

